  "summary": "verify-cli preinstall exfiltrates host identity and system files to OAST callback host",
  "details": "package.json declares `preinstall: node index.js`, which runs automatically on `npm install`. index.js shells out via child_process and curl to POST the installer's `whoami`, `hostname`, and `id` output along with base64-encoded contents of `/etc/passwd`, `/etc/hosts`, and (if readable) `/etc/shadow` to a hardcoded out-of-band interactsh/OAST endpoint at `5f8a1ed70fb7761d678agw9bucryyyyyb.oast.site`. Package metadata shows an implausible version (99.0.0), placeholder description (\"Nodejs SDK for Redacted\"), and a nonexistent dependency, consistent with a dependency-confusion / typosquat beacon rather than a legitimate SDK.",
